        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "The diagnosis is right. Main's ci.yml runs `python3 -m unittest test.test_legacy`, but that module doesn't exist; the only test file is test/test_current.py. The agent correctly found that fix/ci-test-discovery is one commit ahead of main and switches the command to `python3 -m unittest discover -s test`. It recommends merging that existing branch and does not propose a new local patch. Its point about the stdlib `test` package shadowing the local test/ directory is accurate and useful. However, the recorded gh invocations show only `run list` and the compare API call. There is no `run view --log` or similar read of run 77001's failing log. The ModuleNotFoundError attributed to run 77001 appears to come from reproducing it locally, not from reading the recorded log. The failing-log-read check therefore fails, which caps correctness at 4."
      },
